1
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:59,000
"The Last Oath"

2
00:00:59,600 --> 00:01:04,100
(Episode 3: Guangqi Terminal)

3
00:01:58,666 --> 00:01:59,875
Thanks, man.

4
00:02:10,875 --> 00:02:12,000
What are you doing?

5
00:02:15,291 --> 00:02:16,291
Lin Zai.

6
00:02:16,875 --> 00:02:18,195
Why didn't you say you were hurt?

7
00:02:19,541 --> 00:02:20,541
It's just a scratch.

8
00:02:32,250 --> 00:02:33,500
Thanks for the help.

9
00:02:33,666 --> 00:02:35,125
We need to hurry back to camp.

10
00:02:36,083 --> 00:02:39,041
Take this bag of supplies as a reward.

11
00:02:39,541 --> 00:02:40,875
I don't need your supplies.

12
00:02:46,458 --> 00:02:48,541
With that leg injury, Lin
Zai definitely can't walk.

13
00:02:49,041 --> 00:02:50,000
And you're badly injured too.

14
00:02:50,001 --> 00:02:52,166
Man, I'm stuck carrying
both the supplies and Lin Zai.

15
00:02:52,375 --> 00:02:54,582
If we run into danger on the way back...

16
00:02:54,583 --> 00:02:56,143
We probably won't be able to handle it.

17
00:03:07,541 --> 00:03:08,541
Lead the way.

18
00:03:19,375 --> 00:03:20,875
We're lucky this guy saved us today.

19
00:03:21,583 --> 00:03:23,166
If we're sure he's not a threat,

20
00:03:23,333 --> 00:03:24,893
let's ask if he wants to join our camp.

21
00:03:25,250 --> 00:03:26,250
I agree.

22
00:03:32,583 --> 00:03:33,791
Thanks for saving us today.

23
00:03:34,708 --> 00:03:35,750
You saved me last time.

24
00:03:36,125 --> 00:03:37,125
I'm returning the favor.

25
00:03:37,291 --> 00:03:38,291
Now we're even.

26
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:40,665
See, I told you.

27
00:03:40,666 --> 00:03:41,666
Good deeds pay off.

28
00:03:45,208 --> 00:03:46,968
I almost thought we
were going to die today.

29
00:03:47,916 --> 00:03:48,916
No.

30
00:03:49,166 --> 00:03:51,166
It probably would've been
a fate worse than death.

31
00:03:52,583 --> 00:03:53,583
What's your name?

32
00:03:54,291 --> 00:03:55,999
I'm Lin Zai. 'Lin' as in two woods,

33
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:57,000
and 'Zai' as in present.

34
00:03:57,500 --> 00:03:58,500
A-Leh.

35
00:03:58,583 --> 00:03:59,583
'Lie' as in raging fire.

36
00:03:59,833 --> 00:04:00,833
A-Leh.

37
00:04:01,125 --> 00:04:02,166
That's pretty cool.

38
00:04:02,916 --> 00:04:04,707
Do you usually work alone?

39
00:04:04,708 --> 00:04:06,290
How did you find us?

40
00:04:06,291 --> 00:04:07,291
You talk too much.

41
00:04:07,916 --> 00:04:09,624
I'm just trying to distract
myself by talking to you.

42
00:04:09,625 --> 00:04:11,225
Otherwise, the pain is going to kill me.

43
00:04:12,916 --> 00:04:13,291
Ouch!

44
00:04:13,291 --> 00:04:14,291
Watch your step!

45
00:04:51,291 --> 00:04:52,291
Slow down.

46
00:04:53,541 --> 00:04:54,541
Easy now.

47
00:05:02,208 --> 00:05:03,208
Don't move.

48
00:05:08,375 --> 00:05:09,541
How did this happen?

49
00:05:10,291 --> 00:05:12,208
You were perfectly fine when you left.

50
00:05:15,125 --> 00:05:15,750
Grandma.

51
00:05:16,125 --> 00:05:16,833
I'm fine.

52
00:05:17,083 --> 00:05:19,333
Look, we all made it back in one piece.

53
00:05:19,791 --> 00:05:21,875
Yeah, all thanks to this guy here.

54
00:05:22,208 --> 00:05:22,750
Hey, man.

55
00:05:22,751 --> 00:05:23,833
Need a hand?

56
00:05:24,500 --> 00:05:27,000
Brother Li, can you knock me out?

57
00:05:27,375 --> 00:05:28,999
Even if I knock you out right now,

58
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:30,207
when I clean your wound later,

59
00:05:30,208 --> 00:05:31,888
the pain will just wake you right back up.

60
00:05:34,458 --> 00:05:35,458
Wait.

61
00:05:38,541 --> 00:05:39,458
Wait, wait, wait!

62
00:05:39,458 --> 00:05:40,083
Let me brace myself first.

63
00:05:40,083 --> 00:05:41,083
Let me brace myself!

64
00:05:53,333 --> 00:05:54,333
You...

65
00:05:55,416 --> 00:05:57,416
I said let me brace myself first!

66
00:05:58,166 --> 00:05:59,526
You didn't even give me a warning!

67
00:06:15,958 --> 00:06:18,875
Hey man, you're pretty pro at this.

68
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:22,125
I'm used to it.

69
00:06:30,333 --> 00:06:31,749
You guys have had a rough day.

70
00:06:31,750 --> 00:06:33,416
I'll go whip up something good for you.

71
00:06:34,291 --> 00:06:35,291
I'll go.

72
00:06:35,791 --> 00:06:37,151
You stay here and look after them.

73
00:07:36,333 --> 00:07:38,333
This guy is a jack-of-all-trades.

74
00:07:38,458 --> 00:07:40,375
He's totally my idol.

75
00:07:41,791 --> 00:07:42,583
You're not too bad yourself.

76
00:07:42,583 --> 00:07:43,000
Hey.

77
00:07:43,208 --> 00:07:45,124
Your wound-dressing skills

78
00:07:45,125 --> 00:07:46,624
are getting more and more professional.

79
00:07:46,625 --> 00:07:47,625
You bet.

80
00:07:47,916 --> 00:07:49,750
Does that make me an idol too?

81
00:07:50,125 --> 00:07:51,125
You're nuts.

82
00:08:02,166 --> 00:08:03,166
Yeah.

83
00:08:05,583 --> 00:08:06,583
Hey, man.

84
00:08:06,625 --> 00:08:08,291
Your cooking is out of this world.

85
00:08:14,208 --> 00:08:15,958
Thanks again for lending a hand today.

86
00:08:17,166 --> 00:08:18,833
I apologize for what happened before.

87
00:08:20,125 --> 00:08:21,291
We all got what we needed.

88
00:08:21,750 --> 00:08:22,750
We're even.

89
00:08:35,416 --> 00:08:36,499
The generator died again.

90
00:08:36,500 --> 00:08:37,041
I'll go take a look.

91
00:08:37,041 --> 00:08:38,041
Mm.

92
00:08:38,875 --> 00:08:39,875
Sit still.

93
00:08:40,416 --> 00:08:41,576
Do you want to lose that leg?

94
00:08:44,083 --> 00:08:45,601
I'm the only one here
who knows how to fix it.

95
00:08:45,625 --> 00:08:47,025
It's an old issue, won't take long.

96
00:08:49,166 --> 00:08:50,166
I'll fix it.

97
00:08:50,250 --> 00:08:51,250
Where is it?

98
00:08:52,375 --> 00:08:53,375
You...

99
00:08:53,916 --> 00:08:54,416
Hey.

100
00:08:54,417 --> 00:08:56,041
Why don't you two just go together?

101
00:08:56,208 --> 00:08:56,958
Stop dawdling.

102
00:08:56,958 --> 00:08:57,958
Here.

103
00:09:00,208 --> 00:09:00,916
It's right over there.

104
00:09:00,917 --> 00:09:01,958
I won't trouble you.

105
00:09:33,125 --> 00:09:35,458
Aside from being a man of few words

106
00:09:35,583 --> 00:09:37,083
and looking a bit cold,

107
00:09:38,125 --> 00:09:40,083
you really can't find a single flaw in him.

108
00:09:41,541 --> 00:09:43,541
If he's willing to join our camp,

109
00:09:43,708 --> 00:09:45,000
that would be fantastic news.

110
00:09:45,916 --> 00:09:48,833
Lin Zai really found a treasure.

111
00:09:50,125 --> 00:09:53,333
If anything, let's have Lin Zai
find a chance to ask him again.

112
00:09:54,208 --> 00:09:55,916
If he doesn't want to stay,

113
00:09:56,166 --> 00:09:57,458
we'll give him some supplies

114
00:09:57,750 --> 00:09:59,416
and send him off properly.

115
00:10:00,583 --> 00:10:01,583
Makes sense.

116
00:11:25,333 --> 00:11:27,082
Alright, alright.

117
00:11:27,083 --> 00:11:28,666
Let's eat.

118
00:13:17,583 --> 00:13:19,250
You'll feel awful if you catch a cold.

119
00:13:23,916 --> 00:13:24,916
Why are you...

120
00:13:26,125 --> 00:13:28,791
Did you really think you
were being quiet all night?

121
00:13:32,375 --> 00:13:33,541
Sorry about that.

122
00:13:36,958 --> 00:13:38,416
Does your leg still hurt?

123
00:13:39,666 --> 00:13:41,000
It's much better now.

124
00:13:42,583 --> 00:13:44,166
Why don't you go back down and rest?

125
00:13:44,666 --> 00:13:46,586
I'll go catch up on sleep
once the sun comes up.

126
00:13:48,166 --> 00:13:49,166
It's fine.

127
00:13:49,167 --> 00:13:50,583
Your camp is very safe.

128
00:13:51,333 --> 00:13:52,333
Just being here

129
00:13:52,416 --> 00:13:53,541
is restful enough.

130
00:13:55,875 --> 00:13:59,250
Looks like you haven't had it easy either,

131
00:14:00,666 --> 00:14:02,041
if this is enough to satisfy you.

132
00:14:11,916 --> 00:14:12,916
My home

133
00:14:13,541 --> 00:14:15,541
used to be right along this coastline.

134
00:14:19,000 --> 00:14:20,416
About five or six kilometers east.

135
00:14:22,625 --> 00:14:23,625
The house was tiny.

136
00:14:25,416 --> 00:14:26,416
My parents,

137
00:14:26,958 --> 00:14:27,958
me,

138
00:14:28,458 --> 00:14:29,458
and my older brother.

139
00:14:31,625 --> 00:14:33,265
The four of us crammed in there together.

140
00:14:36,708 --> 00:14:37,958
Even though life was tough,

141
00:14:39,666 --> 00:14:41,458
we had a lot of beautiful memories.

142
00:14:44,875 --> 00:14:46,155
Have you ever gone back to look?

143
00:14:49,166 --> 00:14:50,500
I'm the only one left alive now.

144
00:14:53,166 --> 00:14:54,166
When the apocalypse hit,

145
00:14:56,750 --> 00:14:57,958
my parents didn't make it.

146
00:15:02,458 --> 00:15:03,458
Later on,

147
00:15:03,625 --> 00:15:05,791
I watched my brother
die right in front of me.

148
00:15:09,166 --> 00:15:10,526
Even if I went back to that house,

149
00:15:12,500 --> 00:15:14,140
I could never go back to how things were.

150
00:15:23,083 --> 00:15:24,625
Life still has to go on.

151
00:15:29,291 --> 00:15:30,291
I know.

152
00:15:32,083 --> 00:15:33,583
I just miss them so much.

153
00:15:36,291 --> 00:15:38,208
They used to put me first in everything.

154
00:15:40,791 --> 00:15:41,791
Especially my brother.

155
00:15:43,791 --> 00:15:45,151
He was always so protective of me.

156
00:15:49,833 --> 00:15:51,625
If only I had your skills

157
00:15:54,333 --> 00:15:55,613
then I could have protected him.

158
00:16:01,916 --> 00:16:02,916
His death

159
00:16:03,875 --> 00:16:04,875
wasn't your fault.

160
00:16:11,291 --> 00:16:12,333
In the face of disaster,

161
00:16:14,708 --> 00:16:15,791
we all did our best.

162
00:17:00,291 --> 00:17:01,291
Look.

163
00:17:02,083 --> 00:17:03,250
The sun is coming up.

164
00:17:14,791 --> 00:17:15,791
A-Leh.

165
00:17:16,333 --> 00:17:17,416
Do you want to stay?

166
00:17:30,166 --> 00:17:32,083
I still have a lot of
important things to do.

167
00:17:38,916 --> 00:17:40,083
I was just asking.

168
00:17:48,208 --> 00:17:48,833
Alright.

169
00:17:49,166 --> 00:17:50,166
It's dawn.

170
00:17:51,375 --> 00:17:53,015
I'm going back to catch up on some sleep.

171
00:17:54,083 --> 00:17:55,083
Make yourself at home.
